    "text": "Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mo>:</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi>R</mi></math>&nbsp;be a function defined by :&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfenced open=\"{\" close=\"\"><mtable><mtr><mtd><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>&#8804;</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></munder><mfenced open=\"{\" close=\"}\"><mrow><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>;</mo></mtd><mtd><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8804;</mo><mn>2</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>;</mo></mtd><mtd><mn>2</mn><mo>&#60;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&#60;</mo><mn>3</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mfenced open=\"[\" close=\"]\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>;</mo></mtd><mtd><mn>3</mn><mo>&#8804;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8804;</mo><mn>5</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo></mtd><mtd><mi>x</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mn>5</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable></mfenced></math><br />Where&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mi>t</mi></mfenced></math> is the greatest integer less than or equal to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>t</mi></math>. Let&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi></math> be the number of points where&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi></math> is not differentiable and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>I</mi><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mo>&#8747;</mo><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi></math>. Then the ordered pair&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> is equal to"
